{"page":3,"totalPages":3,"perPage":6,"nextPage":null,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/circle-chords.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/circle-chords.webp\" alt=\"Chords drawn between periodic points on a circle, tracing out a cardioid\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2014-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2014.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/circle-chord-fun\">Fun with circle chords</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Draw a chord from point n to point 2n around a circle, repeat a few hundred times, and a cardioid appears out of nowhere. A small program I wrote so my kids could go hunting for the shapes hiding inside simple arithmetic.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Circle</li><li>Chords</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/Szilard-portrait.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/Szilard-portrait.webp\" alt=\"Portrait photograph of the physicist Leo Szilard\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2014-03-15T00:00:00.000Z\">2014.03.15</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>10 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/leo_szilard\">Leo Szilard - The Man who changed the World</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">He patented the nuclear chain reaction, drafted the letter that Einstein signed, and then spent the rest of his life trying to restrain the weapon he had set in motion. Leo Szilard may be the most consequential physicist you have never heard of.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Leo Szilard</li><li>Fission</li><li>Manhattan Project</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/gravity_train_poster.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/gravity_train_poster.webp\" alt=\"Illustration of a gravity powered train travelling through the Earth\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2014-01-17T00:00:00.000Z\">2014.01.17</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>8 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/gravitytrain\">Gravity Train</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Dig a straight tunnel between any two points on Earth, pump out the air, and let gravity supply the propulsion. The trip takes 42 minutes, and the remarkable part is that it takes 42 minutes no matter which two cities you pick.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Physics</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Gravity</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/corot_ill.jpg\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/corot_ill.jpg\" alt=\"Illustration of a planet close to its star\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2013-12-03T00:00:00.000Z\">2013.12.03</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>6 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/fallingintothesun\">Falling into  the sun</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">The Earth stays in orbit because of its angular momentum. Take that away, stopping the planet dead in its tracks, and how long until it reaches the Sun? Working out the answer turns up an unexpected appearance by pi.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Physics</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Gravity</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}